THOUGHT: I need to modify addFormField so that formBuilder is safely dereferenced without changing other methods. I’ll use sed to replace the existing two lines in addFormField with versions that wrap formBuilder in Objects.requireNonNull, matching the pattern already used elsewhere, and then rebuild to confirm the error count drops by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/retrofit && sed -i '208,214s/@SuppressWarnings("ConstantConditions") // Only called when isFormEncoded was true\.
  void addFormField(String name, String value, boolean encoded) {
    if (encoded) {
      formBuilder.addEncoded(name, value);
    } else {
      formBuilder.add(name, value);
    }
  }/@SuppressWarnings("ConstantConditions") // Only called when isFormEncoded was true.
  void addFormField(String name, String value, boolean encoded) {
    if (encoded) {
      java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(formBuilder).addEncoded(name, value);
    } else {
      java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(formBuilder).add(name, value);
    }
  }/' retrofit/src/main/java/retrofit2/RequestBuilder.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "DEREFERENCE_NULLABLE" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

